  <p class="gd-byline" style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--blue-soft);opacity:.9;margin:16px 0 0">By <a href="/about" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Heliski Travel Team</a> · Updated 17 Aug 2026</p>
  <p class="gd-lede">For strong, advanced skiers, the appeal of heli-skiing is the terrain no lift can reach: steep couloirs, big open faces and committing lines on snow no one else has touched. Iceland's Troll Peninsula has plenty to offer at this end of the spectrum, handled with the judgement that steep skiing demands. This guide covers the steep terrain, the ability it requires, how guides manage it, and how to progress onto it safely, before you look at <a href="/packages">the packages</a>.</p>
